cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use tcpcat in your research or tooling, please cite it."
title: "tcpcat: know what your servers expose"
abstract: >-
  tcpcat checks what the servers and networks you are responsible for expose.
  It scans them from the outside (SYN, connect and UDP scans, service, version
  and OS detection, an eBPF/AF_XDP engine), and its offline AI explains each
  open port: what it is, why it matters and how to fix it, verifying its own
  findings with read-only follow-up probes. It ties each port to the program
  behind it, correlates vulnerabilities with distribution patch data, checks
  exposure against YAML rules from several vantage points, and keeps signed
  evidence that can be replayed to verify a fix. Reports are JSON, SARIF and
  HTML.
type: software
authors:
